    ("식은 죽 먹기", "이 정도 문제는 식은 죽 먹기예요.", "i jeongdo munjeneun sigeun juk meokgiyeyo.",
     "Soal begini sih gampang banget.", "A problem like this is a piece of cake.",
     "Sopan (해요체). Harfiah 'makan bubur yang sudah dingin', artinya sangat mudah. Sinonim: 누워서 떡 먹기.",
     "Polite (해요체). Literally 'eating cold porridge': very easy. Synonym: 누워서 떡 먹기."),
    ("그림의 떡", "돈이 없으니 저 차는 그림의 떡이에요.", "doni eopseuni jeo chaneun geurimui tteogieyo.",
     "Nggak punya uang, mobil itu cuma angan-angan.", "With no money, that car is just pie in the sky.",
     "Sopan (해요체). Harfiah 'kue beras dalam lukisan': diinginkan tapi tak bisa didapat. Mirip 'bagai pungguk merindukan bulan'.",
     "Polite (해요체). Literally 'rice cake in a painting': something you want but can't have."),
    ("미역국을 먹다", "운전면허 시험에서 또 미역국을 먹었어요.", "unjeonmyeonheo siheomeseo tto miyeokgugeul meogeosseoyo.",
     "Saya gagal lagi di ujian SIM.", "I failed my driving test again.",
     "Sopan (해요체). Harfiah 'makan sup rumput laut' (licin, 'tergelincir'), artinya gagal ujian. Karena itu dihindari sebelum ujian, padahal wajib saat ulang tahun.",
     "Polite (해요체). Literally 'eat seaweed soup' (slippery), meaning fail an exam. Avoided before exams, yet eaten on birthdays."),
    ("바람을 맞다", "어제 소개팅에서 바람을 맞았어요.", "eoje sogaetingeseo barameul majasseoyo.",
     "Kemarin saya ditinggal nggak datang di kencan buta.", "I got stood up on a blind date yesterday.",
     "Sopan (해요체). Artinya janji tidak ditepati dan ditunggu sia-sia. Pelakunya: 바람을 맞히다. Jangan tertukar dengan 바람을 피우다 (selingkuh).",
     "Polite (해요체). To be stood up. The one who does it: 바람을 맞히다. Don't confuse with 바람을 피우다 (to cheat)."),
    ("국수를 먹다", "두 사람 언제 국수를 먹여 줄 거예요?", "du saram eonje guksureul meogyeo jul geoyeyo?",
     "Kalian berdua kapan nikahnya?", "So when are you two getting married?",
     "Sopan (해요체). Harfiah 'makan mi', artinya menikah, karena pesta nikah dulu menyajikan 잔치국수. 국수를 먹여 주다 = mengundang ke pernikahan.",
     "Polite (해요체). Literally 'eat noodles', meaning to marry, since weddings served 잔치국수. 국수를 먹여 주다 = invite someone to your wedding."),
    ("시치미를 떼다", "네가 먹은 거 다 알아. 시치미를 떼지 마.", "nega meogeun geo da ara. sichimireul tteji ma.",
     "Aku tahu kamu yang makan. Jangan pura-pura nggak tahu.", "I know you ate it. Don't play dumb.",
     "Santai (반말). Artinya pura-pura tidak tahu. Sopan: 시치미 떼지 마세요. Dalam percakapan 를 sering dihilangkan.",
     "Casual (반말). To feign ignorance. Polite: 시치미 떼지 마세요. 를 is often dropped in speech."),
    ("한턱내다", "승진했으니까 오늘은 제가 한턱내겠습니다.", "seungjinhaesseunikka oneureun jega hanteongnaegetseumnida.",
     "Karena saya naik jabatan, hari ini saya yang traktir.", "I got promoted, so today's on me.",
     "Formal (합니다체). Artinya mentraktir untuk merayakan sesuatu. Teman sering menagih: 한턱 쏴! (traktir dong!).",
     "Formal (합니다체). To treat people to celebrate something. Friends demand: 한턱 쏴!"),
    ("파김치가 되다", "야근을 해서 파김치가 되었어요.", "yageuneul haeseo pagimchiga doeeosseoyo.",
     "Habis lembur, badan rasanya remuk.", "After working overtime, I'm completely wiped out.",
     "Sopan (해요체). Harfiah 'jadi kimchi daun bawang' yang layu, artinya sangat lelah. Bentuk lisan biasa: 파김치가 됐어요.",
     "Polite (해요체). Literally 'become wilted green-onion kimchi': exhausted. Spoken form: 파김치가 됐어요."),
    ("오지랖이 넓다", "옆집 아줌마는 오지랖이 넓어서 남의 일에 다 참견해요.", "yeopjip ajummaneun ojirapi neolbeoseo namui ire da chamgyeonhaeyo.",
     "Ibu sebelah suka ikut campur urusan orang.", "The lady next door is nosy and meddles in everyone's business.",
     "Sopan (해요체). Harfiah 'kelepak bajunya lebar', artinya suka mencampuri urusan orang. Bernada kritik; jangan dipakai langsung ke orang yang lebih tua.",
     "Polite (해요체). Literally 'one's coat flap is wide': meddlesome. Critical; don't say it to an elder's face."),
    ("산통을 깨다", "깜짝 파티인데 산통을 깨지 마.", "kkamjjak patiinde santongeul kkaeji ma.",
     "Ini pesta kejutan, jangan dibocorkan.", "It's a surprise party, don't spoil it.",
     "Santai (반말). Artinya menggagalkan rencana yang hampir berhasil. Sopan: 산통을 깨지 마세요.",
     "Casual (반말). To ruin a plan that was going well. Polite: 산통을 깨지 마세요."),
    ("김칫국부터 마시다", "아직 발표도 안 났는데 김칫국부터 마시지 마세요.", "ajik balpyodo an nanneunde gimchitgukbuteo masiji maseyo.",
     "Pengumumannya saja belum keluar, jangan kegeeran dulu.", "The results aren't even out yet; don't count your chickens.",
     "Sopan (해요체). Harfiah 'minum kuah kimchi duluan' sebelum kuenya datang. Dari peribahasa 떡 줄 사람은 생각도 안 하는데 김칫국부터 마신다.",
     "Polite (해요체). Literally 'drink the kimchi broth first' before the rice cake arrives. From 떡 줄 사람은 생각도 안 하는데 김칫국부터 마신다."),
    ("찬물을 끼얹다", "모두 신났는데 그 말이 찬물을 끼얹는 바람에 조용해졌어요.", "modu sinanneunde geu mari chanmureul kkieonneun barame joyonghaejyeosseoyo.",
     "Semua lagi senang, tapi omongan itu bikin suasana langsung dingin.", "Everyone was excited, but that remark threw cold water on it.",
     "Sopan (해요체). Harfiah 'menyiram air dingin', artinya merusak suasana atau semangat orang.",
     "Polite (해요체). Literally 'splash cold water': kill the mood or dampen enthusiasm."),
    ("물 건너가다", "비자가 안 나와서 여행 계획은 물 건너가 버렸어요.", "bijaga an nawaseo yeohaeng gyehoegeun mul geonneoga beoryeosseoyo.",
     "Visanya nggak keluar, rencana liburan pun batal total.", "The visa didn't come through, so the trip plan is dead.",
     "Sopan (해요체). Harfiah 'sudah menyeberang air', artinya sudah tak mungkin lagi. Biasanya bentuk lampau: 물 건너갔다.",
     "Polite (해요체). Literally 'crossed the water': no longer possible. Usually past tense: 물 건너갔다."),
    ("뜸을 들이다", "뜸을 들이지 말고 빨리 말해 봐.", "tteumeul deuriji malgo ppalli malhae bwa.",
     "Jangan bertele-tele, cepat bilang.", "Stop keeping me in suspense and just say it.",
     "Santai (반말). Asalnya dari menanak nasi (membiarkan nasi matang dengan uap), artinya mengulur waktu. Sopan: 뜸 들이지 말고 말해 주세요.",
     "Casual (반말). From cooking rice (letting it steam), meaning to drag things out. Polite: 뜸 들이지 말고 말해 주세요."),
    ("하늘의 별 따기", "요즘 서울에서 집 구하기는 하늘의 별 따기예요.", "yojeum seoureseo jip guhagineun haneurui byeol ttagiyeyo.",
     "Sekarang cari rumah di Seoul susahnya minta ampun.", "Finding a home in Seoul these days is next to impossible.",
     "Sopan (해요체). Harfiah 'memetik bintang di langit', artinya hampir mustahil. Pola: N은/는 하늘의 별 따기다.",
     "Polite (해요체). Literally 'picking a star from the sky': nearly impossible. Pattern: N은/는 하늘의 별 따기다."),
    ("우물 안 개구리", "외국에 나가 보니 제가 우물 안 개구리였더라고요.", "oeguge naga boni jega umul an gaeguriyeotdeoragoyo.",
     "Setelah ke luar negeri, saya sadar selama ini saya katak dalam tempurung.", "Going abroad made me realize I'd been a frog in a well.",
     "Sopan (해요체). Harfiah 'katak dalam sumur', persis 'katak dalam tempurung': orang berwawasan sempit.",
     "Polite (해요체). Literally 'a frog in a well': someone with a narrow worldview."),
    ("바닥이 나다", "월말이라 통장 잔고가 바닥이 나서 라면만 먹어요.", "wolmarira tongjang jangoga badagi naseo ramyeonman meogeoyo.",
     "Akhir bulan, saldo rekening habis, jadi makan mi instan saja.", "It's the end of the month and my bank balance has run dry, so I'm living on ramen.",
     "Sopan (해요체). Harfiah 'sampai ke dasar', artinya habis (uang, stok, tenaga). Mirip 'kantong kering'.",
     "Polite (해요체). Literally 'hit the bottom': run out (money, stock, energy)."),
    ("진땀을 빼다", "면접에서 어려운 질문 때문에 진땀을 빼고 왔어요.", "myeonjeobeseo eoryeoun jilmun ttaemune jinttameul ppaego wasseoyo.",
     "Di wawancara kerja, saya keringat dingin karena pertanyaan sulit.", "I was sweating bullets over tough questions at the interview.",
     "Sopan (해요체). Harfiah 'mengeluarkan keringat kental', artinya kewalahan atau sangat gugup. Variasi: 진땀이 나다.",
     "Polite (해요체). Literally 'shed thick sweat': struggle hard or be very nervous. Variant: 진땀이 나다."),
    ("엎질러진 물", "이미 엎질러진 물이니까 너무 자책하지 마세요.", "imi eopjilleojin murinikka neomu jachaekaji maseyo.",
     "Nasi sudah menjadi bubur, jangan terlalu menyalahkan diri.", "It's no use crying over spilled milk, so don't blame yourself too much.",
     "Sopan (해요체). Harfiah 'air yang sudah tumpah', persis 'nasi sudah menjadi bubur'.",
     "Polite (해요체). Literally 'spilled water': what's done can't be undone."),
    ("뒷북을 치다", "다 끝났는데 이제 와서 뒷북을 치네.", "da kkeunnanneunde ije waseo dwitbugeul chine.",
     "Semua sudah selesai, baru sekarang heboh.", "It's all over and only now you react.",
     "Santai (반말). Harfiah 'memukul gendang belakangan', artinya bereaksi atau mengabarkan hal yang sudah basi. Sopan: 뒷북을 치시네요 (tetap menyindir).",
     "Casual (반말). Literally 'beat the drum afterward': react to old news. Polite: 뒷북을 치시네요 (still teasing)."),
    ("바가지를 긁다", "아내가 매일 바가지를 긁어요.", "anaega maeil bagajireul geulgeoyo.",
     "Istri saya mengomel setiap hari.", "My wife nags me every day.",
     "Sopan (해요체). Harfiah 'menggaruk gayung', artinya istri mengomeli suami. Jangan tertukar dengan 바가지를 쓰다 (kena getok).",
     "Polite (해요체). Literally 'scrape a gourd': a wife nagging her husband. Don't confuse with 바가지를 쓰다 (get ripped off)."),
    ("바가지를 쓰다", "관광지에서는 바가지를 쓰기 쉬우니까 가격을 먼저 물어보세요.", "gwangwangjieseoneun bagajireul sseugi swiunikka gagyeogeul meonjeo mureoboseyo.",
     "Di tempat wisata gampang kena getok harga, jadi tanya harganya dulu.", "It's easy to get ripped off at tourist spots, so ask the price first.",
     "Sopan (해요체). Artinya membayar jauh di atas harga wajar, mirip 'kena getok'. Pelakunya: 바가지를 씌우다.",
     "Polite (해요체). To pay far more than the fair price. The one doing it: 바가지를 씌우다."),
    ("땡땡이를 치다", "고등학교 때 땡땡이를 치고 바다에 간 적이 있어요.", "godeunghakgyo ttae ttaengttaengireul chigo badae gan jeogi isseoyo.",
     "Waktu SMA saya pernah bolos lalu pergi ke pantai.", "In high school I once skipped class and went to the beach.",
     "Sopan (해요체). Bahasa lisan untuk bolos sekolah atau kerja, lebih santai dari 결석하다. 를 sering hilang: 땡땡이 치다.",
     "Polite (해요체). Colloquial for skipping school or work, more casual than 결석하다. 를 is often dropped: 땡땡이 치다."),
